cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the archived aggregate results, please cite the manuscript and this release."
title: "Two-centre analysis of intraoperative hypotension episode continuity and 48-hour creatinine-defined acute kidney injury (MOVER and VitalDB)"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, locked analysis contract, and aggregate expected results for a
  two-centre retrospective cohort study harmonising the MOVER (United States) and
  VitalDB (South Korea) databases to test whether concentrating 20 minutes of
  intraoperative hypotension into one episode carries greater 48-hour
  creatinine-defined acute kidney injury risk than distributing the same duration
  across four episodes. No patient-level data are included.
